<title>PHILIPPINES: Citra, PNCC secure $262 mln loan.</title>
<headline>Citra, PNCC secure $262 mln loan.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Citra Metro Manila Tollways Corp, a joint venture of Indonesia's Citra Group and the state-run Philippine National Construction Corp, has signed a $262 million loan agreement with 18 local and foreign banks.</p>
<p>The loan will be used to fund in part its $514 million, 35-kilometer elevated highway in Manila, a statement from Citra Metro said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The joint lead arrangers for the $262 million loan are FEB Investments Inc, ING Bank and Urban Corp.</p>
<p>The company also approved the issuance of $60 million convertible preferred shares to the American International Group-Asian Infrastructure Fund (AIG-AIF) to help finance the project. - Manila newsroom 63 2 8418936 fax 8176267</p>
</text>
